  "body": "The spec talks about Document object goes away permanently:\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html#garbage-collection-2\r\n> If a user agent is to forcibly close an EventSource object \\(this happens when a Document object goes away permanently\\), the user agent must abort any instances of the fetch algorithm started for this EventSource object, and must set the readyState attribute to CLOSED\\.\r\n\r\nBut what about Web Workers? In particular this Web Worker code:\r\n\r\n```\r\nself.close();\r\nvar a = new EventSource(\"something\");\r\na.readyState == EventSource.CLOSED\r\n```\r\n\r\nshould the readyState be CLOSED or CONNECTING? Same for:\r\n\r\n```\r\nvar a = new EventSource(\"something\");\r\nself.close();\r\na.readyState == EventSource.CLOSED\r\n```\r\n\r\nI would suggest to change the spec saying: \r\n\r\n> If a user agent is to forcibly close an EventSource object \\(this happens when a Document object goes away permanently or when a Web Worker is closed\\), the user agent must abort any instances of the fetch algorithm started for this EventSource object, and must set the readyState attribute to CLOSED\\.",
